C03: the prohibition «no me digas…» projects to its request head (LIMITS1699)

In SYSTEM1697 the boundary «No me digas la versión de Python.» was not read as a negative constraint: _negative_action_forms projects a prohibited subjunctive to its request head by regular endings and the irregular «digas» became «dige», so the turn went to knowledge conversation and the model answered the previous welcome greeting. «digas» now projects to «dime», like «pongas», «hagas» and «vayas». The language decision and the effect readers over the 742 registry literals are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


